<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>rDownloader packages</title>
<style>
  body { font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 48rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; }
  pre { background: #f4f4f5; padding: 0.75rem; overflow-x: auto; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { background: #18181b; color: #e4e4e7; } pre { background: #27272a; } a { color: #93c5fd; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>rDownloader packages for apt and dnf</h1>
<p>The signed apt and dnf repositories of <a href="https://rdownloader.net">rDownloader</a>, for x86-64 and arm64.</p>
<h2>Debian and Ubuntu</h2>
<pre>sudo install -d -m 0755 /etc/apt/keyrings
curl -fsSL @BASE_URL@/rdownloader.asc | sudo tee /etc/apt/keyrings/rdownloader.asc &gt; /dev/null
curl -fsSL @BASE_URL@/rdownloader.sources | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/rdownloader.sources &gt; /dev/null
sudo apt update
sudo apt install rdownloader</pre>
<h2>Fedora and openSUSE</h2>
<pre>sudo curl -fsSL -o /etc/yum.repos.d/rdownloader.repo @BASE_URL@/rdownloader.repo
sudo dnf install rdownloader
# openSUSE: sudo zypper addrepo @BASE_URL@/rdownloader.repo &amp;&amp; sudo zypper install rdownloader</pre>
<p>Signing key: <a href="rdownloader.asc"><code>@FINGERPRINT@</code></a>. The last @KEEP@ versions of each package stay for a downgrade.
Installation handbook: <a href="https://github.com/degoya/rDownloader/wiki/installation">wiki/installation</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
